//? Title: EfficientNet: Compound Scaling and Visible B0 Optimization
//? Subtitle: Tensor computations, explicit checks and reproducible local figures
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
EfficientNet scales width, repeated depth and input resolution together. We inspect released
coefficients, verify all eight full parameter budgets, demonstrate per-row branch dropout
and explicitly fit the complete B0 network with tensor Adam.
)
\toc

Source example: `examples/cpp/source/nn/1_convolutional_neural_networks/1.4_efficient_and_mobile_architectures/efficientnet.cpp`.

> The method

Compound scaling balances depth, width and resolution rather than increasing only one axis.
For a conceptual scale phi, d=alpha^phi, w=beta^phi and r=gamma^phi with approximate
compute constraint alpha*beta²*gamma²≈2. The released B0-B7 table uses concrete coefficients;
it is that table, rather than a newly searched optimum, that the code executes.

Every B0 stage uses SE .25 with a reduction based on unexpanded input width, swish x*sigmoid(x),
and an expansion-one or expansion-six mobile bottleneck. Widths round to multiples of eight,
with at most ten percent rounding reduction; repeats ceil(depth*base_repeats). Stem and head
widths also scale. A linear projection precedes any raw identity shortcut. The first-repeat
stride downsamples each specified stage; repeated blocks use stride one.

At zero-based block index i of n, matching training residuals drop with probability .2*i/n.
The inverted surviving branch is multiplied by 1/p; inference uses the full branch. Head dropout
comes from the released variant table. The mask fixture checks row sharing and input derivatives,
including p=0 and p=1 endpoints. Branch filters/BN still execute, so dropout alone does not imply
conditional-computation speedup. The B0 CIFAR model has 4020358 learned scalars and sixteen blocks.

All eight FULL-WEIGHT models execute at 64 pixels for counts. Their exact target-resolution
MAC budgets use ceil(resolution/downsampling_divisor) on each SAME map, not a global area
ratio; SE/classifier work stays fixed. B0 additionally executes an actual 224-pixel forward.
The larger models are not claimed to run at their large reference resolutions. A separate full
B0 backward probe retains every channel/block at 64 pixels, freezes moving updates and disables
branch dropout while retaining classifier dropout. Projection BN shifts may cancel through
subsequent pointwise/BN paths, so every gradient must be finite but need not be nonzero.

All model computation, image scaling, augmentation, losses and optimizer updates use tensors.
Architecture strings, integer dimensions and plotted vectors are metadata. Convolutions use
He-uniform initialization and TensorFlow SAME padding, BN epsilon 1e-3 with learned scale/shift,
and a biased classifier. Training uses batch moments; inference uses saved moving moments.
Dropout draws from the learned store's generator. The arithmetic log counts convolution,
pooled SE and classifier products, excluding BN, pooling, activations, additions and memory
traffic. One MAC is a multiply-accumulate pair, not measured latency or individual FLOPs.

The bounded fit uses original 32×32 CIFAR-10 images, changes only the stem stride and class
count, and retains every block and channel width. It shows 8 epochs (64 updates, kept short so the report
builds quickly), batch eight, Adam(.001),
explicit kernel L2=.0001/2 and independent padded crops/flips. Fixed subsets contain 64 fit,
32 validation and 32 official-test rows. The lowest validation NLL selects paired learned/BN
checkpoints before test scoring. No accuracy threshold is imposed on this small single-seed
experiment; it is not the published ImageNet training schedule or a latency search.

The editable concept diagram is `diagrams/efficientnet_concept.tikz`. Regeneration uses
LaTeX with PGF/TikZ and standalone, plus dvisvgm; exports use the saved SVG.

```{bash, results="output", file="figures/efficientnet_concept.svg"}
set -eu
mkdir -p build
latex -interaction=batchmode -halt-on-error -output-directory=build diagrams/efficientnet_concept.tikz > build/efficientnet_concept.compile.log 2>&1
dvisvgm --no-fonts --bbox=10 --output=build/efficientnet_concept.svg build/efficientnet_concept.dvi > build/efficientnet_concept.render.log 2>&1
printf 'Rendered local concept diagram.\n'
```
